# The box: Width and Height measure the box with its padding and its border, without its margin.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: The box · Width and height
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: row
			Gap: 24
			Vertical: top
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 18 0
		For style: demo
			Box:
				Background: tint
				Border color: accent
	Section:
		Text: The box
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Width and height
		Paragraph: Without `Width`, a box takes the width its parent leaves and, without `Height`, the height of its content. A declared `Width` or `Height` includes the padding and the border, so the three boxes below measure the same 140 by 60 points.
			Style: intro
		Text: (no Width, no Height)
			Style: label
		Paragraph: This paragraph takes the whole width and the height of its two lines of text. Its background shows its box, which ends where the text of the second line ends.
			Style: demo
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 18 0
		Stack:
			Style: row
			Item:
				Block:
					Text: Width: 140, Height: 60
						Style: label
					Block:
						Style: demo
						Box:
							Width: 140
							Height: 60
						Text: content 140 × 60
			Item:
				Block:
					Text: + Padding: 10
						Style: label
					Block:
						Style: demo
						Box:
							Width: 140
							Height: 60
							Padding: 10
						Text: content 120 × 40
			Item:
				Block:
					Text: + Padding: 10, Border: 5
						Style: label
					Block:
						Style: demo
						Box:
							Width: 140
							Height: 60
							Padding: 10
							Border: 5
						Text: content 110 × 30
		Text: Width: 50%, Height: 40
			Style: label
